Specifically:

* The `gpui` crate (https://crates.io/crates/gpui), used as this application's
  UI framework and consumed as a published dependency.

* `crates/app/src/composer.rs` is adapted from `crates/gpui/examples/input.rs`
  in the Zed repository. GPUI ships no text-input widget, so the example is the
  reference implementation for cursor movement, selection, clipboard handling,
  grapheme boundaries, IME integration, and the custom text `Element`. Our
  version adds Enter-to-submit, cross-platform key bindings, dark-theme colours,
  a disabled state, and avoids let-chains (edition 2021). See the file header.

